## Installation

Clone the repository:

git clone https://github.com/yourusername/veyra.git
cd veyra

Veyra uses only Python's standard library, so no external packages are required.

Recommended Python version:

Python 3.10+

## Configuration

Create a `config.json` file:

{
    "timeout": 10,
    "retries": 2,
    "endpoints": [
        {
            "name": "API",
            "url": "https://api.example.com",
            "expected_status": 200
        },
        {
            "name": "Website",
            "url": "https://example.com",
            "expected_status": 200
        }
    ]
}

## Usage

Run the monitor:

python veyra.py

Generate a custom report:

python veyra.py --config config.json --output report.json

Example output:

{
    "timestamp": "2026-09-21T11:30:00+00:00",
    "total": 2,
    "healthy": 2,
    "failed": 0,
    "endpoints": [
        {
            "name": "API",
